# Writing Intelligence — ignore rules
#
# The governing distinction: the semantic state is canonical and renderings are
# builds (Law M). Everything a build produces is derivable and does not belong
# in git. The small set of files that declare intent — project, tests, policy,
# and the lockfile that pins what a release was built from — are the parts you
# commit, and they are unignored explicitly below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Workspace state — local build state, not source
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .wi/ holds the object store, graph, refs, decisions, judgments, snapshots,
# attestations, builds, reports, cache and workspace.db. All of it is
# reconstructible and all of it is machine-local. wi.project.yaml,
# wi.tests.yaml, wi.policy.yaml and wi.lock live outside it and are committed.
.wi/
!wi.lock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build outputs and renderings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A rendering is compiled from state. Committing one creates a second writable
# source of truth, which is the exact failure Law M exists to prevent.
outputs/
dist/
build/

# Proof capsules are release artifacts. They are published on a release page,
# not carried in the tree, and a stale capsule in a repo is a proof of a state
# that no longer exists.
*.wic

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Simulation and candidate state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A candidate root exists only to be compared and then discarded. If one of
# these files reaches a commit, something wrote what it promised not to write.
*.candidate.json
*.simulation.json
.wi-scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# wi.py working files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.original-*
*.claims.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reference runtime (services/api) — optional, not required to run the tool
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
services/api/node_modules/
services/api/*.log
services/api/dist/
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local configuration — never committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
